{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Mama kept her Bible on the win[G]dowsill by the sink
Pa[Bm]ges soft as flour sacks and underlined [G]in pencil ink
She said, child, when the [Bm]road forks and you don't know where to go
[G]There's a word I want you holding more than a[Bm]nything you know
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Trust in the LORD [G]with all your heart
And do not lean on [G]your own under[D]standing
In all [Bm]your ways acknowledge him
[A]And he will make your [G]paths straight
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I've been [D]lost on county [Bm]highways with a [A]map ac[D]ross my knee
Sure that I was smart [G]enough to find the way for [D]me
[Bm]But the roads I chose kept winding and [G]the dust got in my [D]eyes
Till I pulled [Bm]off on the shoulder and I let go [G]of my pride
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Trust in [D]the LORD with [Bm]all your heart
And do not lean on [G]your own understand[D]ing
In all your [G]ways acknowledge [D]him
And he will [Bm]make your paths [A]straight
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Do not be [G]wise in your own [D]eyes
Fear the LORD [Bm]and turn away [A]from e[G]vil
Bind them around your neck
[D]Write them on the tablet of [Bm]your heart
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Trust [A]in [G]the LORD with all your heart
[D]And do not lean on [A]your own understanding
In all your [G]ways acknowledge [D]him
And he will [Bm]make your paths [A]straight
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
He will make [G]your paths [D]straight
Mama, I [Bm]still hear you [A]say
{end_of_verse}

